  "summary": "Six preprints from 18–24 November pair FRB dispersion-measure cosmology with quantified CMB biases from CO emission, birefringence and polarization calibration.",
  "synthesis": "Two strands share a focus on forward modeling for survey analyses. Fast radio burst work uses dispersion measures as a cosmological probe: IllustrisTNG-based mapping of baryon density across large-scale structure, a first Ωm–w inference from 125 localized bursts alone, and a tentative 143 pc cm^-3 excess toward DESI galaxy groups from 117 localized FRBs. The CMB papers quantify systematics: an analytic halo model for CO and CO×CIB as a foreground, with ~2σ parameter bias in CMB-HD-like settings; polarization-angle calibration transfer between Simons Observatory LAT and SAT; and positive small-scale lensing bandpower bias from unmodeled anisotropic birefringence, addressed by joint MUSE estimation. The strands are linked by method rather than data. The group-excess result is tentative, and the FRB cosmological constraints rest on a cosmology-dependent DM model.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
